# Short owned trust component names

One storage-only candidate follows the sealed CString baseline. A private
invocation-local 32-byte array handles names shorter than 32 bytes; all longer
names retain CString conversion. Short embedded-NUL inputs return the same
Invalid before open, without creating a discarded owned error. Empty, Unicode,
slash/dot and arbitrary-length compatibility remain. The array is not total
enum/stack footprint. No path rule, observation, cache or authority changes.

`check.ps1 -Lane host|194|188 -Cohort <new-name>` refuses existing logs. Host
runs 31 source canaries and affected all-target check/strict all-feature lint.
GNU/MSRV each run five new pure controls, five unchanged trust baseline controls,
four earlier stack controls, five document baseline controls and two counter
controls, then affected check/lint. No ignored test or live File/clock/Probe/
openat is invoked by the controls; ordinary-user WSL supplies Rust build/units.

The actual helper supplies bytes and pointer to a pure adapter. Complete-body
models retain parent/flags, one callback, NUL priority, error/File schedule and
no EINTR retry. Seed 0x074c57a1 matches the baseline's 512 schedules; boundary,
long-NUL/fallback, input mutation, move and nested independent values are also
checked. Synthetic callbacks are not real descriptor or filesystem fault proof.

Both first Linux compiles refuse two legacy tests' inherited CString imports
after removal of the production import. Keep the initial source/guard and logs.
The corrected cohort retains that import only under cfg(test), and updates only
its exact source reversal. The name algorithm and live body remain the same.

After the exact source commit, `review.ps1 -Mode Seal -Source <40-hex-commit>`
creates fsynced metadata once. `review.ps1 -Mode Review` checks it offline,
including eight earlier raw seals/348 members and matching frozen baseline
counters. No historical source-pinned reviewer is modified.

This measures Rust allocation requests, not full preparation latency, CPU/RSS or
retention. Original windows 300/60/10 seconds and both first Causal refusals
